WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.260
After his return from Monkey City, Mowgli lived happily among the wolf pack.

2
00:00:07.261 --> 00:00:12.187
He grew taller and stronger.

3
00:00:12.188 --> 00:00:15.987
He hunted and swam.

4
00:00:15.988 --> 00:00:27.676
He sat in the sun, and he ate and slept—then ate and slept again.

5
00:00:27.677 --> 00:00:35.576
At Council Rock the wolves often asked Mowgli to pull sharp thorns from their paws.

6
00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:39.376
Mowgli noticed something strange whenever he did it.

7
00:00:39.377 --> 00:00:44.372
If he stared at the wolves, they quickly looked away.

8
00:00:44.373 --> 00:00:52.004
"That's odd," he thought. "Are the wolves afraid of me?"

9
00:00:52.005 --> 00:00:56.331
Mowgli sometimes saw Shere Khan in the jungle.

10
00:00:56.332 --> 00:00:59.368
Mowgli tried to keep his distance.

11
00:00:59.369 --> 00:01:04.238
But many of the young wolves were growing loyal to Shere Khan.

12
00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:07.849
The tiger tossed them scraps of food.

13
00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:10.191
He praised them too.

14
00:01:10.192 --> 00:01:16.549
"What fine, brave hunters you are!" Shere Khan purred.

15
00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:20.076
"I don't know why you let Akela lead you.

16
00:01:20.077 --> 00:01:24.170
He's getting so old and weak."

17
00:01:24.171 --> 00:01:28.922
"Mowgli might lead the pack one day," a young wolf said.

18
00:01:28.923 --> 00:01:31.746
"The man cub is very smart."

19
00:01:31.747 --> 00:01:37.254
"He can even remove thorns from our paws," another wolf said.

20
00:01:37.255 --> 00:01:41.339
"That man cub again!" Shere Khan growled.

21
00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:45.164
"He is no better than any of you!"

22
00:01:45.165 --> 00:01:48.210
Some of the wolves growled too.

23
00:01:48.211 --> 00:01:52.951
"You're right, Shere Khan. Mowgli is not even a wolf!"

24
00:01:52.952 --> 00:01:56.978
Bagheera watched what was happening within the wolf pack.

25
00:01:56.979 --> 00:02:00.858
And he didn't like it.

26
00:02:00.859 --> 00:02:07.931
"Mowgli, how many times have I told you that Shere Khan is your enemy?" he asked one afternoon.

27
00:02:07.932 --> 00:02:12.593
The two friends were lying on some leaves in the warm sun.

28
00:02:12.594 --> 00:02:19.658
Mowgli laughed. "As many times as there are nuts on that tree!"

29
00:02:19.659 --> 00:02:21.371
He shook his head.

30
00:02:21.372 --> 00:02:25.587
Bagheera was always giving him warnings and advice.

31
00:02:25.588 --> 00:02:29.065
"Well, listen carefully," Bagheera said.

32
00:02:29.066 --> 00:02:34.456
"Akela is getting old. Soon he will be too weak to lead the pack.

33
00:02:34.457 --> 00:02:37.986
That's when the younger wolves will take action.

34
00:02:37.987 --> 00:02:41.572
They will try to throw you out of the pack."

35
00:02:41.573 --> 00:02:47.567
"They won't throw me out of the pack!" Mowgli was still laughing.

36
00:02:47.568 --> 00:02:51.749
"I live in the jungle. I obey its law.

37
00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:56.625
I even pull thorns from my brothers' and sisters' paws."

38
00:02:56.626 --> 00:03:00.359
"Those things are true," Bagheera said firmly.

39
00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.197
"But you're not a wolf.

40
00:03:02.198 --> 00:03:03.654
You're a human.

41
00:03:03.655 --> 00:03:06.387
And someday you will live among them."

42
00:03:06.388 --> 00:03:12.844
"I don't think so, Bagheera." Mowgli yawned.

43
00:03:12.845 --> 00:03:17.988
"Sometimes I go to the hill to look down at the people's village.

44
00:03:17.989 --> 00:03:20.728
But I never talk to the villagers.

45
00:03:20.729 --> 00:03:23.387
I don't hunt with them.

46
00:03:23.388 --> 00:03:27.274
Anyway, you've lived in the jungle for your whole life.

47
00:03:27.275 --> 00:03:30.716
You don't know anything about people."

48
00:03:30.717 --> 00:03:34.323
The panther shifted his paws and looked away.

49
00:03:34.324 --> 00:03:37.200
"I'm sorry to say this," he said.

50
00:03:37.201 --> 00:03:40.366
"But most of the wolves hate you.

51
00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:43.549
They think you're wiser and stronger than they are.

52
00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:46.893
That's why they look away when you stare at them.

53
00:03:46.894 --> 00:03:49.547
They are your enemies."

54
00:03:49.548 --> 00:03:56.446
"What?" Mowgli felt stung, as if a bee had landed on his skin.

55
00:03:56.447 --> 00:04:04.105
He leaped up. "I thought they were my friends! Bagheera, what should I do?"

56
00:04:04.106 --> 00:04:07.488
"You must protect yourself," Bagheera said.

57
00:04:07.489 --> 00:04:11.827
"Akela is not going to be able to lead the pack for much longer.

58
00:04:11.828 --> 00:04:16.317
As soon as he fails at hunting, the young wolves will turn against him.

59
00:04:16.318 --> 00:04:22.202
They'll go to Council Rock, and—I've got it!" Bagheera smiled.

60
00:04:22.203 --> 00:04:26.053
"You must go down to the humans' village in the valley.

61
00:04:26.054 --> 00:04:30.066
Get some of the red flower, which they grow there."

62
00:04:30.067 --> 00:04:34.416
"The red flower?" Mowgli repeated.

63
00:04:34.417 --> 00:04:39.569
Every beast in the jungle lived in fear of the humans' fire.

64
00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:43.756
"The red flower grows outside their huts at twilight.

65
00:04:43.757 --> 00:04:45.916
I could try to get some."

66
00:04:45.917 --> 00:04:48.677
"Good!" Bagheera nodded.

67
00:04:48.678 --> 00:04:51.236
"Get it quickly and keep it nearby.

68
00:04:51.237 --> 00:04:59.699
When the time comes, you will be ready with a mighty weapon."

